# Veripsa release gate (auto-discovered). One gate per file -> two PRs adding gates add two FILES, never a
# shared line -> no false merge conflict on registration. register_gate is defined in run_gates.sh.
# Format: register_gate <test> <marker> <name> <ok_blurb> <desc> [tail]
register_gate "tests/test_fork_neighbor_refresh_leak.py" "FORK-NEIGHBOR-REFRESH GATE: PASS" "fork-neighbor refresh info-leak (privacy fix)" "fork-neighbor refresh info-leak closed (audit r3 privacy launch-blocker): the is_fork redaction protected the ACTING fork PR's own comment, but the NEIGHBOR-refresh path (_refresh_changes -> _post_refreshes, fired on open/sync/merge/withdraw/push) re-rendered every OTHER in-flight change and posted it to THAT PR's conversation WITHOUT is_fork -- so a fork PR that was an in-flight neighbor received the FULL comment (other base-repo PR refs / author logins / paths / symbols) on the EXTERNAL contributor's conversation. The engine/DB has NO fork concept (content-free), so the fix resolves fork status from GitHub at POST time: _refresh_changes carries both the full comment AND a redacted fork_* variant, and _post_refreshes selects it for an external-readable neighbor while non-fork maintainer PRs still get full detail. The production REST read now returns confirmed_fork separately from redact_external: head.repo=null for a deleted fork selects redaction but does not disable required-check or pause behavior; complete equal ids remain non-fork and unredacted. Proven end-to-end on a production-realistic impact (no injected fork flag): the redacted variant is content-free, the full comment keeps detail, and _post_refreshes posts the redacted comment to the fork neighbor -- RED on origin/main (the neighbor's posted comment leaks), GREEN after" "fork-neighbor refresh info-leak closed: a fork PR that is an in-flight neighbor gets the REDACTED refresh comment, unknown identity also redacts without weakening merge gating, non-fork maintainer PRs keep full detail; content-free" 24
